{
  "question": "Why was rubber chosen for the remote control?",
  "answer": "The provided evidence segments do not state that rubber was chosen for the remote control, nor do they provide any reasons for choosing it. Segment 4 only lists rubber as one of the material options being considered [Seg 4]. Therefore, the evidence is insufficient to answer why rubber was chosen.",
  "evidence_graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "seg_008",
        "text": "Wood looks premium but it's heavy and expensive. I'd rule that out.",
        "speaker": "ID",
        "start_time": 43.5,
        "end_time": 49.0,
        "weight": 0.14675557613372803,
        "entities": [
          "wood",
          "premium",
          "heavy",
          "expensive"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_007",
        "text": "The target demographic is adults aged twenty-five to forty who watch a lot of television.",
        "speaker": "ME",
        "start_time": 36.5,
        "end_time": 43.0,
        "weight": 0.13118882477283478,
        "entities": [
          "target demographic",
          "adults",
          "television"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_013",
        "text": "For colors, I'd recommend black, silver, and maybe a bold red option.",
        "speaker": "UI",
        "start_time": 75.5,
        "end_time": 81.0,
        "weight": 0.07687114924192429,
        "entities": [
          "colors",
          "black",
          "silver",
          "red"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_002",
        "text": "I've been looking into materials. We have three options: plastic, rubber, and wood.",
        "speaker": "ID",
        "start_time": 5.5,
        "end_time": 11.0,
        "weight": 0.06090452894568443,
        "entities": [
          "materials",
          "plastic",
          "rubber",
          "wood"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_006",
        "text": "We also need to consider the button layout. I suggest a simple ergonomic design.",
        "speaker": "UI",
        "start_time": 30.5,
        "end_time": 36.2,
        "weight": 0.05392581224441528,
        "entities": [
          "button layout",
          "ergonomic design"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_009",
        "text": "I agree. So it's between plastic and rubber. Given the user preference data, I vote rubber.",
        "speaker": "PM",
        "start_time": 49.5,
        "end_time": 56.0,
        "weight": 0.04103265702724457,
        "entities": [
          "plastic",
          "rubber",
          "user preference"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_001",
        "text": "Okay, let's start the meeting. Today we need to decide on the remote control design.",
        "speaker": "PM",
        "start_time": 0.0,
        "end_time": 5.2,
        "weight": 0.03867024928331375,
        "entities": [
          "remote control",
          "design"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_004",
        "text": "From a cost perspective, plastic is the cheapest option at two euros per unit.",
        "speaker": "ID",
        "start_time": 18.0,
        "end_time": 24.3,
        "weight": 0.03660774603486061,
        "entities": [
          "cost",
          "plastic",
          "two euros"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_003",
        "text": "The market research shows that users prefer a comfortable grip, which points to rubber.",
        "speaker": "ME",
        "start_time": 11.5,
        "end_time": 17.8,
        "weight": 0.03257283940911293,
        "entities": [
          "market research",
          "users",
          "grip",
          "rubber"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_014",
        "text": "The battery compartment needs to be easily accessible. Maybe a slide-off back panel.",
        "speaker": "ID",
        "start_time": 81.5,
        "end_time": 87.0,
        "weight": 0.029164409264922142,
        "entities": [
          "battery compartment",
          "back panel"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_011",
        "text": "Alright, let's go with the rubber casing. The small cost difference is worth it for the user experience.",
        "speaker": "PM",
        "start_time": 62.5,
        "end_time": 69.0,
        "weight": 0.02852031961083412,
        "entities": [
          "rubber casing",
          "cost difference",
          "user experience"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_010",
        "text": "The rubber material also has better drop resistance, which is important for remote controls.",
        "speaker": "ID",
        "start_time": 56.5,
        "end_time": 62.0,
        "weight": 0.02118263579905033,
        "entities": [
          "rubber",
          "drop resistance",
          "remote controls"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_012",
        "text": "Next item: we need to finalize the color options. Marketing suggests trendy colors.",
        "speaker": "PM",
        "start_time": 69.5,
        "end_time": 75.0,
        "weight": 0.020997345447540283,
        "entities": [
          "color options",
          "marketing",
          "trendy colors"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_005",
        "text": "But the rubber casing is only slightly more expensive, about two fifty per unit.",
        "speaker": "ID",
        "start_time": 24.5,
        "end_time": 30.1,
        "weight": 0.01874363236129284,
        "entities": [
          "rubber casing",
          "two fifty"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "seg_015",
        "text": "Good point. We'll use double-A batteries since they're widely available.",
        "speaker": "PM",
        "start_time": 87.5,
        "end_time": 92.0,
        "weight": 0.012978745624423027,
        "entities": [
          "double-A batteries"
        ]
      }
